<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy — FerrFlow"
  description="What FerrFlow does (and doesn't) send to our servers. The CLI is fully offline; cloud features are opt-in."
  lang="en"
  canonical="https://ferrflow.com/privacy"
  pathname="/privacy"
  lastUpdated="2026-05-01"
  draft
>
  <span slot="heading">Privacy — <em>FerrFlow</em></span>

  <h2>The FerrFlow CLI</h2>
  <p>
    The CLI binary <strong>does not send any data to FerrLabs servers</strong>. It reads
    your local commits, bumps version files, generates changelogs, creates git tags and
    GitHub releases (calling the GitHub API on your behalf with <em>your</em> token).
    No telemetry, no error reporting, no auto-update check, no usage stats.
  </p>
  <p>
    The only network traffic FerrFlow makes is what you ask it to: pulling git remotes,
    pushing tags, posting to GitHub Releases, optionally publishing to package registries.
  </p>

  <h2>The marketing site (ferrflow.com)</h2>
  <p>
    Read-only marketing pages. No analytics tracker. No cookie set by FerrFlow itself.
    See <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>FerrFlow Bot (optional GitHub integration)</h2>
  <p>
    The FerrFlow Bot is a GitHub App that automates version bumps and releases on PRs.
    When you install it on a repository, FerrLabs receives:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Webhook events from GitHub: PR open / merge, push events on default branch.</li>
    <li>The metadata necessary to compute the next version: commits SHAs, commit messages, conventional-commits trailers, branch refs.</li>
    <li>A short-lived OAuth token with the scope you grant: read commits, write tags, write releases on the chosen repositories.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    No source code body, no diff content, no issue / PR description body is read or
    stored. The bot processes events in-memory and writes back the version bump as a new
    commit and tag, without persisting your data beyond logs (30 days retention).
  </p>

  <h2>Cloud account (app.ferrlabs.com)</h2>
  <p>
    Account, billing and team management are governed by the canonical
    <a href="https://ferrlabs.com/privacy">FerrLabs privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <p style="margin-top:48px;font-size:13px;">
    French version: <a href="/fr/privacy">Confidentialité</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
